WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Heat pumps are the future of residential HVAC. R-410A replacements are all heat
pump compatible.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Manual J calculates the heating and cooling load of a building based on
insulation, windows, orientation, climate, and occupancy. The result determines
the correct equipment size in tons (1 ton = 12,000 BTU/hr). Oversized equipment

00:00:40.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Manual J: ACCA load calculation determining required heating and cooling
capacity.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Ton: Unit of cooling capacity. 1 ton = 12,000 BTU per hour.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Short Cycling: System turning on and off too frequently. Caused by oversized
equipment.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Understanding load calculations helps you
identify improperly sized systems — a common cause of comfort complaints.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Watch out for these: Bigger is NOT better — oversized systems cause humidity
problems. And — 1 ton = 12,000 BTU/hr

00:02:40.000 --> 00:03:00.000
